from pathlib import Path
import json
root=Path('reports/synthetic_accounting_sanity')
summary=json.loads((root/'summary.json').read_text());rows=json.loads((root/'all_cases.json').read_text())
html=r'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>SHIELD — 5,000 synthetic accounting tests</title>
<style>body{margin:0;background:#fafafa;color:#202020;font:15px/1.5 system-ui,sans-serif}main{max-width:1450px;margin:auto;padding:30px}h1{font-size:26px;margin-bottom:6px}h2{font-size:20px}p{max-width:1050px}.muted{color:#646464}.summary{display:flex;gap:35px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:26px 0}.metric strong{display:block;font-size:25px}.notice{background:#fff6dd;padding:15px;border-left:4px solid #9b7200}.controls{display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;padding:16px 0}label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;font-size:12px}select,input,button{font:inherit;padding:8px;border:1px solid #ccc;border-radius:4px;background:white;color:inherit}button{cursor:pointer}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:12px;background:white}th,td{text-align:left;padding:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;vertical-align:top}th{position:sticky;top:0;background:#eee}td.num{white-space:nowrap;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.wrap{overflow:auto;max-height:680px;border:1px solid #ddd}tr.selected{background:#fff3b0}.pill{font-weight:600}.detail{padding:20px;background:white;border:1px solid #ccc;margin:20px 0}dl{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(220px,1fr));gap:10px}dt{color:#666;font-size:12px}dd{margin:0;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.barline{display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr 100px;gap:15px;margin:9px 0;align-items:center}.track{background:#e8e8e8;height:14px}.bar{height:14px;background:#6e6e6e}.pagination{display:flex;gap:15px;align-items:center;margin:15px 0}footer{margin-top:30px;color:#666;font-size:12px}a{color:#245a90}h3{font-size:16px}</style>
<main><div class="muted">SHIELD · Offline model sanity audit · 29 October 2026</div><h1>Five accounting amounts → seven raw ratios → model response</h1><p>5,000 generated scenarios. Assumed raw minimum 0 and maximum 1 for every feature, making the normalisation formula an identity. The exact saved seven-feature Random Forest was used. No dataset or test rows were read.</p><div class="notice"><strong>This is a heuristic consistency test, not an accuracy evaluation.</strong> There are no known bankruptcy outcomes for these invented companies. “Counterintuitive” means the model response conflicts with the stated screening expectation; it does not prove the correct original scaling or guarantee how a real company should be classified. All cases contain at least one raw ratio outside the model columns’ observed 0–1 range; no clipping was applied.</div>
<div class="summary" id="metrics"></div><h2>Paired directional results</h2><p class="muted">Bar length = percentage of 1,000 pairs where the score fell by more than 0.2 percentage points. Lower score is the stated screening expectation after an improvement, not a universal financial law.</p><div id="bars"></div><p class="muted">X-axis: score-decrease percentage (0–100%). Y-axis: controlled scenario change. Source: generated cases, seed 42, current saved RF.</p>
<h2>Inspect every case</h2><p>Choose filters or click a case to see all five accounting amounts, the seven values sent to the model and the verdict explanation. There are 100 cases per page.</p>
<div class="controls"><label>Verdict<select id="verdict"><option value="">All</option><option>counterintuitive</option><option>consistent</option><option>unchanged</option><option>inconclusive</option></select></label><label>Variant<select id="variant"><option value="">All</option><option>base</option><option>profit_up</option><option>debt_down</option><option>retained_up</option><option>combined_improvement</option></select></label><label>Starting profile<select id="profile"><option value="">All</option><option>strong</option><option>weak</option><option>mixed</option></select></label><label>Case or base ID<input id="search" placeholder="e.g. B0001"></label><button id="download">Download filtered CSV</button></div>
<div id="detail" class="detail"></div><div class="pagination"><button id="prev">Previous</button><span id="page"></span><button id="next">Next</button></div><div class="wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Case / starting profile</th><th>Net income (RM)</th><th>Assets (RM)</th><th>Liabilities (RM)</th><th>Equity (RM)</th><th>Retained earnings (RM)</th><th>Score / band</th><th>Change vs base (pp)</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody id="body"></tbody></table></div>
<h2>How the expectations were defined</h2><ul><li><strong>Strong baselines (400):</strong> net income/assets 10–25%, liabilities/assets 5–30%, retained earnings/assets 10–40%, positive equity. Expected screen Low Risk (below 30%).</li><li><strong>Weak baselines (400):</strong> losses/assets 5–20%, liabilities/assets 85–150%, accumulated losses. Expected screen High/Critical Risk (60% or above). These are heuristic scenario labels, not bankruptcy outcomes.</li><li><strong>Mixed baselines (200):</strong> indicators conflict; absolute verdict is inconclusive.</li><li><strong>Profit up:</strong> add profit equal to 5% of assets while other accounting amounts remain fixed.</li><li><strong>Debt down:</strong> decrease liabilities/assets by roughly 15 percentage points (floor 1%) and increase equity to preserve A=L+E. Avoid zero-equity division. This is a matched static profile, not a simulated loan repayment.</li><li><strong>Retained earnings up:</strong> increase by up to 10% of assets, capped below equity. Other amounts fixed; this implies different equity composition.</li><li><strong>Combined:</strong> apply the three changes together.</li><li><strong>Directional verdict:</strong> decrease &gt;0.2pp = consistent; increase &gt;0.2pp = counterintuitive; change within ±0.2pp = unchanged/inconclusive.</li></ul>
<h2>Limits and reproducibility</h2><ul id="limits"></ul><p id="model"></p><footer>All observations are synthetic and are not advice for actual lending. The website was not changed. Full audit files: all_5000_cases.csv, all_cases.json, summary.json and RESULTS.txt. Run tools/synthetic_ratio_sanity.py to reproduce.</footer></main>
<script>
const summary=__SUMMARY__,data=__DATA__;let page=0,filtered=data,selected=data[0].case_id;const amountKeys=['net_income','total_assets','total_liabilities','equity','retained_earnings'];const labels=['Net income','Total assets','Total liabilities','Equity','Retained earnings'];const featureNames=["Net Income to Stockholder's Equity","Net Income to Total Assets","Retained Earnings to Total Assets","Debt ratio %","Net worth/Assets","Equity to Liability","Liability to Equity"];const fmt=n=>Number(n).toLocaleString('en-MY',{maximumFractionDigits:2});const esc=s=>String(s).replaceAll('&','&amp;').replaceAll('<','&lt;').replaceAll('>','&gt;').replaceAll('"','&quot;');
const low=data.filter(r=>r.screen_band==='Low Risk').length;document.getElementById('metrics').innerHTML=[['Scenarios',data.length],['Starting profiles',summary.base_profiles],['Low Risk outputs',low],['Strong baselines outside Low Risk',summary.group_results['base/strong'].verdicts.counterintuitive]].map(([l,n])=>`<div class="metric"><span>${l}</span><strong>${fmt(n)}</strong></div>`).join('');
document.getElementById('bars').innerHTML=['profit_up','debt_down','retained_up','combined_improvement'].map(v=>{const r=summary.group_results[v+'/all'],n=r.verdicts.consistent||0,p=100*n/r.count;return `<div class="barline"><span>${v.replaceAll('_',' ')}</span><div class="track"><div class="bar" style="width:${p}%"></div></div><span>${p.toFixed(1)}% (${n})</span></div>`}).join('');document.getElementById('limits').innerHTML=summary.limitations.map(s=>'<li>'+esc(s)+'</li>').join('');document.getElementById('model').textContent=`Model: ${summary.model_file}. SHA256: ${summary.model_sha256}. sklearn runtime ${summary.sklearn_runtime}; artifact-version warnings are recorded in summary.json.`;
function detail(id){const r=data.find(x=>x.case_id===id);if(!r)return;selected=id;document.getElementById('detail').innerHTML=`<h3>${esc(r.case_id)} · ${esc(r.verdict)}</h3><p><strong>${r.score_pct.toFixed(2)}% · ${esc(r.screen_band)}</strong> | base ${r.base_score_pct.toFixed(2)}% | change ${r.change_pp.toFixed(2)} percentage points</p><p>${esc(r.reason)}</p><dl>${amountKeys.map((k,i)=>`<div><dt>${labels[i]} (RM)</dt><dd>${fmt(r[k])}</dd></div>`).join('')}</dl><h3>Seven inputs sent unchanged to RF</h3><dl>${featureNames.map(k=>`<div><dt>${esc(k)}</dt><dd>${Number(r[k]).toPrecision(8)}</dd></div>`).join('')}</dl><p class="muted">${r.outside_dataset_unit_range} of 7 inputs outside [0,1]. This is an extrapolation warning, not a reason to clip them silently.</p>`;}
function render(){const start=page*100;document.getElementById('page').textContent=`${filtered.length.toLocaleString()} matching cases · page ${page+1} of ${Math.max(1,Math.ceil(filtered.length/100))}`;document.getElementById('prev').disabled=page===0;document.getElementById('next').disabled=start+100>=filtered.length;document.getElementById('body').innerHTML=filtered.slice(start,start+100).map(r=>`<tr class="${r.case_id===selected?'selected':''}"><td><button data-case="${r.case_id}">${esc(r.case_id)}</button><br>${r.profile}</td>${amountKeys.map(k=>`<td class="num">${fmt(r[k])}</td>`).join('')}<td>${r.score_pct.toFixed(2)}%<br>${r.screen_band}</td><td class="num">${r.change_pp.toFixed(2)}</td><td class="pill">${r.verdict}</td></tr>`).join('');document.querySelectorAll('[data-case]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>{detail(b.dataset.case);render()});}
function filter(){const v=document.getElementById('verdict').value,t=document.getElementById('variant').value,p=document.getElementById('profile').value,q=document.getElementById('search').value.toLowerCase();filtered=data.filter(r=>(!v||r.verdict===v)&&(!t||r.variant===t)&&(!p||r.profile===p)&&(!q||r.case_id.toLowerCase().includes(q)));page=0;render();}
['verdict','variant','profile','search'].forEach(id=>document.getElementById(id).addEventListener('input',filter));document.getElementById('prev').onclick=()=>{page--;render()};document.getElementById('next').onclick=()=>{page++;render()};document.getElementById('download').onclick=()=>{const keys=Object.keys(data[0]),quote=x=>'"'+String(x).replaceAll('"','""')+'"',text='\uFEFF'+[keys.map(quote).join(','),...filtered.map(r=>keys.map(k=>quote(r[k])).join(','))].join('\r\n');const url=URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([text],{type:'text/csv;charset=utf-8'})),a=document.createElement('a');a.href=url;a.download='SHIELD_synthetic_filtered_cases.csv';a.click();setTimeout(()=>URL.revokeObjectURL(url),1000)};detail(selected);render();
</script></html>'''
html=html.replace('__SUMMARY__',json.dumps(summary).replace('<','\\u003c')).replace('__DATA__',json.dumps(rows).replace('<','\\u003c'))
(root/'REPORT.html').write_text(html,encoding='utf-8')
print('Created searchable report with',len(rows),'cases; bytes',len(html.encode()))
